      "id": "a1vsjbu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The President is the supreme commander of the defence forces and the head of the Indian State.",
        "The Presidential election is conducted through an electoral college consisting of elected members of Parliament and State Legislative Assemblies.",
        "Candidates must be Indian citizens, at least 35 years old, and qualified to be elected as a Lok Sabha member.",
        "The President exercises executive, legislative, financial, judicial, and emergency powers as prescribed by the Constitution.",
        "Impeachment proceedings under Article 61 require a 14-day advance notice and a two-thirds majority of the total membership in both Houses."
      ],
      "id": "ib0mlcd"
    },
